WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.825
Cloud PKI is Microsoft's hosted PKI,
managed in the Intune admin center.

2
00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:09.744
For device certificates, it
replaces the on-premises CA,

3
00:00:09.744 --> 00:00:12.725
the NDES server and the
connector in one go.

4
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:17.808
It issues client certificates to
Intune-enrolled devices through SCEP,

5
00:00:17.808 --> 00:00:21.875
publishes its own CRLs, and
hosts up to three CAs per tenant.

6
00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:24.050
Just as important is what it can't do.

7
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.950
It can't issue to anything not enrolled
in Intune, and Intune doesn't manage

8
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:34.413
Windows Server, so no domain controller or
web server gets a Cloud PKI certificate.

9
00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:39.664
It doesn't do PKCS or OCSP, and a CA's
purposes can't change after creation,

10
00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:43.376
so plan your three CAs
before you create anything.

11
00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:47.763
On licensing and government
availability, the slide has the details.

12
00:00:47.763 --> 00:00:50.380
Confirm the entitlement
on your current plan.
